WEBVTT

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.660
Lister, have you ever been hit over the head with a welding mallet?

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.260
No? Just shut up and push the troll.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.320
Yes, sir! Remember!

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.670
Right, corridor 159.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.420
Lister, shut up! I'm only woman.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.260
Well, don't!

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.120
Lister, don't hum and don't make any stupid sounds with your cheeks.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.460
Lister, one more sound, anything, and you're on report, Milano.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.090
What job number's this?

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:49.680
Right, that's it.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:59.380
Lister, the third technician, offence, obstructing a superior technician by humming, clicking, and being quiet.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.980
When the captain sees this, you're dead.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.600
Remember, I'm bored.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.440
Bored? This is essential routine maintenance.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.960
It's absolutely vital for the well-being of this crew, this mission, and this ship.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.390
Dispenser 172. Chicken soup nozzle clogged.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.600
Pass me a 14B, Lister.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.090
Lister, is this a 14B?

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.300
Does it look even remotely like a 14B?

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.560
This is a 14B, Lister.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.170
This is a 14F.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:40.730
Are you blind?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.390
Who cares?

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.090
I care, Lister.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.360
It's my career, Lister.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.800
I'm the one who gets it in the neck if an officer comes along,

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:52.980
orders chicken soup,

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.890
and gets blackcurrant cordial with blancmange and two creams and a sugar.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:09.240
Yep, that's working.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.200
It's stupid anyway, all this maintenance business.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.940
The only reason they don't give this job to the service robots

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.780
is they've got a better union than us.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.140
Listen, that is absolute nonsense.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.430
Right, what's next?

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.090
Botanical Gardens, Faulty Porous Circuit and Corridor 147, Sticking Door.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:29.970
Do you know a...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.980
So, Rimmer, you rank below all four of those service robots, even the one that's gone absolutely mad.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.390
Well, Lister, walk for long, matey. Up, up, up. That's where I'm going.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.710
Not until your passion engineer's exam. And you won't do that because you'll just go in there and flunk again.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.100
Lister, last time I only failed by the narrowest of narrow margins.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:54.120
You what? You walked in there and wrote, I am a fish, 400 times, with a funny little dance and fainted.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.500
That's a total lie.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.480
No, it's not. Peterson told me.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.260
No, it's not. Peterson told me.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.900
If you must know, what I did was I wrote a discourse on porous circuits

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.270
which was simply too radical, too unconventional,

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.550
too mould-breaking for the examiners to accept.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.150
Yeah, he said you were a fish.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.540
Is that a cigarette you're smoking, Lister?

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:14.640
No, it's a chicken.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.380
Right, you're on report.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.480
Two times in as many minutes, Lister, I don't know.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:20.820
Rimmer, Lister?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:21.600
Yes, sir.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.480
Yo, Todd, want to get down?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:25.160
Indeed.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.900
Now, Rimmer, I'm just going through McIntyre's artefacts

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.980
and I see that you've filed two hundred and...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.740
147 complaints against Lister.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.380
Yes, sir.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.340
That's 123 counts of insulting a superior technician,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.120
39 counts of dereliction of duty,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.220
84 counts of general insubordination,

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.500
and one count of mutiny.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.100
Yes, sir.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:47.650
Mutiny, Lister.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:48.820
Still on his top.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.760
Maliciously and with intent to wound.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:51.960
It was an accident.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.360
Lister, I put it to you.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.940
How is it possible to stand on one small toe by accident?

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.180
You didn't stand on my toe at all.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.740
You stood on my entire foot,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:04:59.960
thereby obstructing your support.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.240
technician in pursuit of vital duty. But the vital duty wasn't going to snap my guitar in half?

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.500
Whereupon you leapt from the top bunk onto the hole of my right foot.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.260
Alright, that's enough. Had there been a crisis situation, Lister, I would have had to perform my duties hopping.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.870
Clearly putting the ship at risk, clearly therefore mutiny.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:18.210
Finished? However, I'm not a vindictive man, so I don't intend to apply for the death penalty.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:23.800
There are 169 people on board this ship. You, Rimmer, are over one man. Why can't you two get on?

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:29.980
You see, I try, sir. I'm not an insubordinate man by nature. I try and expect Rimmer and everything, but it's not...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.110
easy because he's such a smeghead? Did you hear that, sir? Listen, do you have any conception

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:43.460
of the penalty for describing a superior technician as a smeghead? Oh, Rimmer. You are a smeghead.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:54.080
Respect, sir. Your career's over, tot, until you finish, you big-leg. We're all gathered here

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.720
today to pay our last respects to George McIntyre. George was an excellent officer and as good a

00:05:59.720 --> 00:05:59.920
friend

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.280
anyone could ever hope to have and he'll be missed more deeply and more completely than he

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:13.270
could ever know and now commend his ashes to the stars he loves so much bye george i'll miss you

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:23.020
this is a piece of music he specially requested start the tape please holly

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:38.910
McIntyre. Bye George. That was George. Really? I thought it was Mary Queen of Scots.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:48.060
Hey, I was watching that. Well tough. You touch that guitar Lister, I'll remove the E string and garrotte you with it.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.250
Can I do anything? Is it okay to breathe? Can I breathe?

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.910
Lister, I have an exam tomorrow which I intend to pass. I know, yeah, by cheating. This is not cheating.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.940
It's merely an aid to memory.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.880
Helps me marshal the facts already in my command.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.900
It does copy the entire textbooks onto your body.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.080
Why don't you hand your body in and let them mark that?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.460
Listen, do you think it's easy for someone like me to become an officer?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.620
Someone who wasn't academy educated?

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.800
Someone who didn't have the right knobby background?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.730
Someone who didn't have the right parents?

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:23.230
You didn't have the right parents?

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.840
Whose parents did you have?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.420
My parents.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.440
The wrong parents.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.980
I'm just saying, you know, if you can't...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.800
Pass fair and square, why bother?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.980
Well, you would, Lister, because you've got no ambition, no drive.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.520
You're perfectly content to be the lowest rank on this ship.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.400
I'm not the lowest rank on this ship.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.270
What about the laboratory mice?

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.350
Tell those mice to do something, they've got to jump to it.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.970
Yes, Mr. Lister, sir!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.760
Lister, you are a nothing.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:51.960
I'm not a nothing, I've got me plan.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.530
What's that, the plan to be the slobbiest entity in the entire universe?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.360
No, me five-year plan.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:07:59.970
You see, I'm going to do two more...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.000
And I've been saving up all my pay.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:02.980
Since when?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:03.980
Since always.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:07.940
That's why I never buy any soap or deodorants or socks or anything like that, you know?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.480
Anyway, I'm going to have a little farm on Fiji.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.460
I'm going to get a sheep and a cow and breed horses.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.500
With a sheep and a cow?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.250
No, with horses and horses.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:21.460
On Fiji?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.180
Yeah, the prices there are unbelievable.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:27.840
Yes, because they had a volcanic eruption and now most of Fiji's three feet below sea level.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.660
It's only three feet they can wade.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.760
That's why the animals are going to have to be quite tall.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.600
Nice plan, Lister. Excellent plan. Brilliant plan, Lister.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.090
What about the sheep? What are you going to do, buy them water wings?

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.440
Fit them with stilts?

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:48.580
Better still, you could crossbreed them with dolphins and have leaping mutton.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:51.920
Babs! Babs!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.290
We get a drainage grant these days.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.490
Why bother, Lister? You could be the first man to produce wet-look knitwear.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.350
This is why I never, ever said anything to you,

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.970
because I knew you'd say something like this.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.310
Lister, you've got the brain of a cheese sandwich.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.710
Morning, Farmer Lister.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.470
I'm just popping down to the shops in my submarine.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:12.610
Can I buy you anything?

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.180
Welcome back.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.200
George McIntyre reception is about to begin in the refectory.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.520
George says he'd like to invite everybody,

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.240
especially those who weren't able to attend his funeral.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.860
I'm waiting for it to come out on paperback!

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:56.950
I've been showing this great new intelligence test, what have you got to do?

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.960
Force the coin onto your forehead, and then the more-

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.240
times you can bang yourself on the head without it falling off. The more intelligent you are,

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:11.640
you've got to go for it. He's going for it. You ready? Yep. Can you feel it? Yep. Can you feel

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:29.050
it? Yep. Go on. Go on. Folks, today is a day for both sadness and joy. Sadness for the passing

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:29.790
away of George.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.890
joy, because George is back with us, albeit as a hologram. Now, some of you may not have

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.710
traveled with a hologram before, so I ask you to treat him as a normal man, because

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:45.030
he is in every respect like George. He has George's personality and George's knowledge

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:50.000
and experience. Of course, he can't lift anything or touch anything, so I ask you to

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:55.340
cooperate with his request. And please, take every care not to walk through him, not even

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.640
when you're in a hurry. Thank you.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:09.650
I want to thank everybody for giving me such a marvellous funeral

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.690
and just seeing the vid.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.800
And I want to thank the captain for his beautiful eulogy.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:16.590
Beautiful.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.020
But I still don't understand why he didn't use the one I wrote.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.840
This must seem pretty spooky for everyone.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.970
But I don't want you to...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.800
think of me as someone who's dead more as someone who's no longer a threat to

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:45.340
marriages hey I think Joe knows what I'm talking about as you know Holly is only

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:50.990
capable of sustaining one hologram so my advice to anyone more vital to the

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:53.570
mission than me is if you die I'll kill you

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.170
for the cutting of the cake.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.280
Flight coordinator George McIntyre.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.180
George!

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.560
Just one thing before the disco.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.500
Holly tells me that he sensed

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.180
a non-human life form aboard.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:27.220
Say it, it's Rimmer!

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.840
We don't know what it is, listen.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.840
So just be careful, okay?

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.340
I'm turning you in, Rebecca.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:41.380
Right, they're bound to ask the right thigh, which is 10%.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:45.400
They must ask the left thigh, which is 20%.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.850
They've got to ask one of the forearms,

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.270
which means I've passed already.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.530
Anything on the left chin is a bonus.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:57.720
Right, cutie, current under tension is...

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:58.650
What's this?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:12:59.970
Current under tension is...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.440
Current under-tension is expandable. Current under-tension is expensive.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:10.000
What does this mean? What does any of this mean?

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:16.060
I've covered my body in complete and utter and total absolute nonsense gibberish!

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:26.960
Plus 20% of the ship's course minus the pi-thigris theorem

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.980
multiplied by 2 over the x-axis minus 1 equals the total volume...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.480
which means I know everything about astroengineering.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.820
Good morning, Lister, for probably the last time.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.650
You got it all down, have you, Rimmer?

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.520
Couple of blanks, but I think we'll do.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.260
So you can't remember any?

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:44.510
Think what you will, Lister.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.110
F-I-S-H, that's how you spell fish.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:51.430
And you just keel over, I'm sure it'll all come flooding back to you.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.270
Dry up, Lister.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.250
Will entrance for the engineer's examination

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.890
now make their way to the teacher?

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:08.230
It's all right, Lister. I'm in complete and total control.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:17.410
Lock.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:18.920
Lock?

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.950
Frankenstein? Come on, Frankenstein.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.080
Oh, you're getting really big now, you know.

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.730
I hope it's not twins, you've already got all my milk ration.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:53.130
Never mind, when the baby cat comes, maybe we can give them water and pretend it's milk that's only a baby cat.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.950
I won't know, eh? Eh? Do you want to see any picture of Fiji again, Frankie?

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.190
You're gonna love it there. Look!

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:07.040
Okay, everybody, you've got three hours.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.780
No modems, no speaking slide rules.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.060
Turn over and start. Good luck.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:01.690
I don't know.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:40.840
Hi, where's the captain's office?

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.480
Over there, where it says captain's office.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.180
Where it's always said captain's office.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:48.610
So that's the captain's office. So how are you then?

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.710
Hi. Do you know what he wants to see me for?

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.600
Yes, I think you've been promoted to Admiral.

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:55.230
Oh, yeah? What?

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:58.290
For your diligence and general devotion to duty.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:16:59.270
Oh, yeah?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:07.050
Lister, you asked to see me, Captain.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:09.160
Where's the cat?

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:10.780
What?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:12.400
What cat?

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:15.820
Lister, not only are you so stupid,

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.060
you bring aboard an unquarantined animal

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:20.520
and jeopardize every man and woman on this ship.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:24.900
Not only that, but you take a photograph of yourself with the cat

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:27.300
and send it to be processed in the ship's lab.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:29.980
Now, I'm going to ask you...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:39.120
again. Do you have a cat? No. Have you got a cat? It's that one. Where'd you get it? Titan? Don't you

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:43.140
realize that that thing could be carrying anything? Don't you remember what happened on the

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:48.260
Oregon with the rabbits? Lister, a loose animal aboard the ship could get anywhere. It could get

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:53.140
into the air ducts. It could get into Holly. You know, a little nibble here and a little nibble

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:58.350
there, Lister, and before you know it, we're flying backwards. Now, I want that cat, and I want

00:17:58.350 --> 00:17:59.530
now. Sit.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.210
Just suppose I did have a cat.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.460
Just suppose, what would you do with Frankenstein?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.600
I'd send it down to the medical centre

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.500
and I'd have it cut up and test run on it.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.640
Would you put it back together when you'd finished?

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.660
Lister, the cat would be dead.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.400
So with respect, sir, what's on it for the cat?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.700
Lister, give me that cat!

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:21.300
It's not as easy as that.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:24.040
Me and the cat, we're going to have a baby cat

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.660
and we're going to buy a farm on Fiji

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.960
and we're going to have a sheep and a cow and three horses.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:29.720
It's me plan.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.530
And no one can get in the way of it, not even you, and I do respect you.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:34.500
Say?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:39.820
Listen, do you want to go into stasis for the rest of the trip and forfeit 18 months' wages?

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:40.340
No.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.000
Do you want to hand over that cap?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:42.560
No.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:44.200
Shoes.

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.530
Look, Dave, no one wants to go through with this.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:49.870
It's okay, I can handle it.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.140
Remember, are you all right?

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.360
I can't really remember. I think I did quite well.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:00.810
Has this gone ahead?

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.620
Haven't you ever travelled interstellar?

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.080
No.

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:04.200
Ah, you don't feel a thing.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:07.020
The stasis room creates a static field of time.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.550
See, just as X-rays can't pass through lead,

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.530
time cannot penetrate the stasis field.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.250
So, although you exist, you no longer exist in time,

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:15.870
and for you, time itself does not exist.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:17.710
You see, although you're still a mass,

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.650
you are no longer an event in space-time,

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.030
you are a non-event mass with a quantum probability of zero.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.490
How simple is that, eh?

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.780
I'm ready.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.090
See you in 18 months.

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:29.970
Holly, I...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.740
Activate the stasis field.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:31.870
Ok, Fred.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.620
It is now safe for you to emerge from stasis.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:57.830
Haven't you just got in?

00:19:58.200 --> 00:19:59.960
Please proceed to the drive room 40...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:07.720
But is everybody hot?

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.060
They're dead, Dave.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:10.980
