00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.220
Everybody, Dave.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:14.760
What, Captain Hollister?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:16.570
Everybody's dead, Dave.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:18.420
What, Todd Hunter?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:20.760
Everybody's dead, Dave.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.930
What, Selby?

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.570
They're all dead. Everybody's dead, Dave.

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:28.390
Peterson isn't, is he?

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:29.960
Everybody is dead.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:59.760
Dave. Not Chen. Gordon Bennett. Yes, Chen. Everybody. Everybody's dead Dave. Rimmer. He's dead Dave. Everybody is dead. Everybody is dead Dave. Wait, are you trying to tell me everybody's dead? Never let him out in the first place. How? Drive plate was inefficiently repaired. It blew and the entire crew was subjected to a lethal dose of cadmium too before I could seal the air in.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.480
Terrible. And why is it so dirty around here? What is this stuff?

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:07.030
That is Catering Officer Olaf Peterson.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:07.770
Come on!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.900
I've been eating half the crew.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.090
And who's that?

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:14.700
That's Captain Hollister.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:15.790
And that's Todd Hunter?

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.890
No, that's Second Technician Rimmer.

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:21.700
Oh, yeah? I didn't recognise him without his report book.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.340
What was Rimmer doing in the drive room?

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:27.880
He was explaining to the captain why he hadn't sealed the drive plate properly.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:29.340
So wait.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.140
How long was I in stasis?

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:36.020
Well, I couldn't release you until the radiation reached a safe background level.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.080
How long?

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:38.890
Three million years.

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.510
Three million years?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.650
I've still got that library book.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.260
What about Chrissy?

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:48.600
What about Chrissy Kachansky?

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:49.790
She's dead, Dave.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.110
Oh, way.

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:56.450
I don't suppose it's any consolation, but if she were still alive, the age difference would be insurmountable.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.070
She was part of me plan.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.630
I never got round to telling her, but she was going to come with me to Fiji.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:05.490
She was going to wear a white dress and ride the horses,

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:07.650
